```java
// Reuse a fixed set of threads via ExecutorService
ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(10);
for (Order order : pendingOrders) {
    pool.submit(() -> orderService.processPayment(order));
}
pool.shutdown();
```
*A bounded pool reuses threads instead of creating thousands, keeping memory and context switching under control.*

